    <!-- Abstract -->
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="">
      <dc:description>
        The Coupling Geometry Surface defines lawful geometric primitives for cross-domain coupling,
        coupling drift channels, coupling stability envelopes, coupling boundary geometry, and
        coupling coherence fields. This surface is strictly additive, geometry-only, and inherits
        exclusively from DSLO v0.7 substrate and manifold lineage. Coupling geometry models lawful
        multi-surface coupling behavior without introducing runtime or agentic behavior.
      </dc:description>
    </rdf:Description>

